      "note": "DiGiCo SD-Rack page and a dealer page (read by a research pass 2026-11-12): 14 card slots (56 in / 56 out), MADI main and aux in / out on BNC, two MADI split outputs, a USB Type B port, dual hot-swap redundant power supplies (the inlets are not named on the DiGiCo page). The size has an assumed axis order (482.7 x 371 x 443.7 mm), so beta-modelled; the ports are the Bêta proposal ports (5 of 9 listed). The real rack carries its I/O on top; the model keeps the rear face. The front is a plain generic panel with card slots drawn. Generic artwork only (content/generic-panels/<id>.json, drawn by npm run asset:panel): connectors, knobs and indicators drawn at the port positions, no photo, no logo, no lettering. Every port and control position is a guess (confidence guess): no drawing or photo was opened."
